    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50040" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">uxorcŭla</span></b> , ae, f.
		dim.
		uxor, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a little wife</i> (ante- and post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">erat ei uxorcula satis quidem tenuis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 9, p. 219, 8</span></i>
			.—As a term of endearment: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mea uxorcula!</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Cas. 4, 4, 19</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">5, 2, 38</span></i>; Varr. ap. <i><span class="en">Non.
				83, 25</span></i>.</div>
